Package: apiplant-slim
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Federico Rampazzo <federico@apiplant.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/apiplant/apiplant
Section: web
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Provides: apiplant
Conflicts: apiplant
Replaces: apiplant
Description: apiplant without TypeScript support (no V8)
 apiplant reads an app directory - resource definitions, functions, an optional
 main.toml - and serves it as an HTTP API, with an admin dashboard, a terminal
 console and a visual editor built into the same binary.
 .
 This is the slim build: the same program compiled without TypeScript support,
 and so without the V8 engine that runs it, which is two thirds of the binary.
 An app whose functions are Rust, C, Zig or Go behaves identically. An app with
 a .ts in functions/ does not: apiplant build refuses to compile it, and
 apiplant run reports the .js it cannot load rather than starting up quietly
 missing an endpoint. `apiplant --version` prints "(slim)".
 .
 The command is still /usr/bin/apiplant, so this package Provides and Conflicts
 with apiplant: installing either replaces the other.
 .
 The package declares no dependencies: the binary links only libc, libm and
 libgcc_s, which are part of every Debian installation. It is built against
 glibc 2.35, so it needs Debian 12 (bookworm) or newer, or Ubuntu 22.04 or
 newer.
